  "prefLabel": "Ins 206.02 Waiver of Procedural Rules",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 206.02 Waiver of Procedural Rules. The hearing officer, upon the hearing officer's own initiative or upon the motion or petition of any interested person, shall waive any requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter not otherwise contrary to law, upon reasonable notice to affected persons, when the proposed waiver appears to be lawful and would be more likely to promote the fair, accurate, and efficient resolution of issues pending before the department than would adherence to a particular rule or procedure.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
